<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Sabca H1 net rises 26 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian Sabca H1 net rises 26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Non-consolidated, unaudited results for six months to June 30, 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated):</p>
<p>    Net profit			  99  vs     79</p>
<p>    Turnover/sales		 4,005  vs  4,261</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 149  vs    239</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   171  vs    155</p>
<p>    Taxes				 73  vs     77</p>
<p>    Investments			 84  vs    117</p>
<p>NOTE - Societe Anonyme Belge de Constructions Aeronautiques (Sabca) is a Belgian aerospace company.</p>
<p>Sabca is 52.96 percent owned by Dassault Belgique Aviation SA, a unit of France's Dassault Industries SA, and 42.80 percent held by the administrators of bankrupt Dutch plane maker Fokker NV.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
